    static String instructions() {
        return "Cite every journal-derived claim wherever it occurs, including Methods, Results context and Discussion. Place [[cite:DOI;pmid:ID]] immediately beside the supported claim; identifiers must resolve to retrieved catalog records. Declare citation_basis: literature for prose relying on publications; study_results, study_design, interpretation or not_applicable distinguish original material. Use citation_policy: strict to reject missing classifications, missing inline citations for literature prose and unplaced references. Original results and declared study definitions do not require invented journal citations. Number references by first appearance, reuse numbers, and link each superscript bracket to the final References section. This follows Nature\'s numerical ordering with user-requested bracketed hyperlinks. A mechanically valid citation does not prove that it supports every sentence; source support, completeness and citation_basis require scientific review.";
