y this study needs to be done and why its answer could matter. Rewrite weak bridges; role labels alone cannot demonstrate persuasiveness. Search the field and similar studies, not only top-hit genes. Include contradictory findings. Use only retrieved, cataloged references for factual and prior-work claims. A bounded, failed or empty search does not establish that no similar research exists; do not assert first-ever novelty. Identify missing coverage as a research need. Citation presence and paragraph-role checks do not verify that a source actually supports a claim. Keep drafting instructions, source-review notes and software/audit details out of finished introduction prose; put unresolved writing/research needs in the review checklist instead of inventing background.";
