prose and incomplete structure; no impact ranking is inferred from analysis type or P-values. These editorial fields enter the hash-approved payload; automatic native inventories do not.\n\nPrincipal-finding depth: finding-discussion-review.html/.yaml audits current paragraph spans, claim-local references, literal short passages, immutable caller-declared public source texts, claim dependencies and eight depth facets across the main text and linked supplements. finding-discussion-template.yaml is a fillable fragment. Review mode preserves legacy drafts with explicit needs; finding_review.mode: strict rejects incomplete mechanical grounding before creating a bundle. Source text scope, provenance, support assessments and scientific sufficiency require review; no word count or literal match certifies truth. Public source snapshots and this automatic review stay local and do not enter the existing editorial payload. Inherited dossiers and source snapshots are rechecked against the current prose.\n\nReproduction: java -jar scripts/jlinalg.jar study manuscript metadata/revision-request.yaml --project \"" + root + "\" --out NEW_BUNDLE --actor-type " + actor.type() + " --actor-id \"" + actor.id() + "\"" + (actor.model() == null ? "" : " --model \"" + actor.model() + "\"") + "\n\nSee software-versions.yaml for exact versions and input/output manifests for SHA-256. All local evidence layers are retained in artifacts/evidence.yaml; original large result tables and public response caches remain in the predecessor project. Keep both bundles together. No patient-level files were copied or read by this revision command. Text fields may still contain sensitive information and must be reviewed before sharing.\n\nHTML editors must not alter this frozen bundle. Revise section IDs in a new revision request and name this manifest plus its SHA-256 as previous_revision to preserve and track prose changes. Manual edits outside that workflow require a separate documented audit trail.\n");
