        h.append("</ul><p>Missing evidence is not negative evidence. When JLinAlg reports exploratory partial-data colocalization, its posterior probabilities are conditional on observed selected variants rather than conventional complete-region evidence. Missing variants, significance filtering, unequal coverage and winner\'s curse can materially bias the result; a null colocalization result is not evidence against a shared causal variant. Candidate counts are not independent instruments or causal estimates. Association and gene-level literature do not establish isoform-specific causality or drug efficacy.</p></details>");
    }
    
    private static String supplement(Map<String, Object> revision, Map<String, Map<String, Object>> evidence, Map<String, Object> catalog, boolean audit) throws IOException {
        StringBuilder h = new StringBuilder(start(audit ? "Evidence and provenance review" : "Supplementary material"));
        StudyCitations citations = new StudyCitations(catalog);
        if (audit) h.append("<p><a href=\"manuscript.html\">Manuscript</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"evidence.yaml\">Complete local evidence snapshot</a></p><p>All current operations are retained, including failed, waiting, null and contradictory evidence. Previews below are not exhaustive result tables. Original manifests record full result paths and hashes.</p><label>Find evidence <input id=\"search\" type=\"search\"></label>");
        h.append("<section class=\"evidence\" id=\"supplemental-table-1\"><h2>Supplemental Table 1. Detailed participant characteristics</h2>").append(StudyPublication.detailedTable1(participantTables(evidence), audit)).append("</section>");
        for (Object raw : list(revision.get("sections"))) {
            /*missing*/ note = map(raw);
            if (!"supplementary".equals(note.get("section"))) continue;
