    private StudyMethods() {
    }
    
    static String instructions() {
        return "Always start Methods with a description of every participating cohort, before any statistical or software description. For established cohorts, retrieve and cite the appropriate design/recruitment paper for each cohort and subcohort; for example, the Framingham Heart Study (FHS), Coronary Artery Risk Development in Young Adults (CARDIA), Women\'s Health Initiative (WHI), and Jackson Heart Study (JHS). Expand names at first use. A cohort paper describes the historical cohort, not this study\'s analysis N, visit, exclusions, consent or phenotype definition. Then describe association, discovery/replication if performed, meta-analysis, enrichment/ontology, Mendelian randomization (MR), network analysis, fine mapping if performed, and colocalization, followed by sensitivity analyses and reproducibility. Describe only analyses actually performed; explicitly distinguish supplied external association results, planned work and blocked analyses. For each performed method give its exact estimator/algorithm, an appropriate retrieved method citation, software/version, inputs, all relevant effective parameters and defaults used, including exact phenotype definitions and comparison operators (for example obesity defined as BMI > 30 kg/m2). State customary values such as FDR < 0.05 without requiring a special justification. Require recorded scientific justifications only for uncommon, study-specific or deviating parameter choices; never invent a rationale. Cite both statistical methods and annotation/database versions where relevant. Association needs model family/link and formula orientation, biological covariates, technical factors, transformations, sample selection/missingness, pedigree/relatedness adjustment and multiple-testing rule. Report any executed effect-outlier QC, its effective thresholds, robust-scale fallback or skipped screening, per-cohort exclusions and resulting testing universe; identify post hoc QC changes and require sensitivity review rather than treating excluded large effects as proven artifacts. Meta-analysis needs effect scale, weighting, fixed/random-effects estimator, heterogeneity and cohort-overlap handling. Describe exact overlap universes, per-source/frozen validation families, missing coverage and direction criteria. Heterogeneity diagnostics need the registered per-feature metric/cutoff, Q correction family, minimum source/feature counts and widespread fraction. Influence comparisons use the declared common feature universe; fewer cohorts or larger Q P values do not establish improved biological homogeneity and cannot select the primary result. Enrichment needs selection threshold, tested-gene universe, feature-to-gene mapping, database/release, test and multiplicity adjustment. MR needs molecular exposure/outcome and tissue, GWAS/QTL sources, instrument P/F thresholds, LD clumping reference/r2/window, allele harmonization, overlap assumptions, estimator and sensitivity settings. GWAS diagnostics need the exact source/contrast and complete versus selected/unknown export, finite natural-log P handling and unresolved zeros, frequency/count/INFO/test strata, observed coordinate/build coverage and display thinning/caps. The median one-df chi-square P transform is descriptive; do not call it proof of confounding, claim LD-adjusted calibration or imply that genomic control changed the original P values. Survival association needs the event/censor definitions and codes, time axis/units, delayed entry, baseline strata, selected participant/event counts, baseline predictors and fixed offsets, exact Cox estimator, tie method and registered LRT or Wald test. State the log-hazard-ratio scale, independent-participant and censoring/PH assumptions, missing-predictor handling and unresolved-fit bounds. Distinguish exact finite-MPLE certificates from numerical convergence; record actual shared cohort-family certificate bounds and holds. Supplied estimates retain upstream attribution. Keep local risk-contrast witnesses and row indices in local supporting artifacts, outside aggregate model packets.  Report log-time efficient PH diagnostics with their separate predictor correction family and nominal global tests; diagnostics do not replace primary association P values or certify assumptions. Subsequent log-HR meta-analysis uses a separate Wald approximation even for source LRTs. Score methods need the outcome and intended use, independent development/tuning/evaluation populations, source-overlap declarations, within-development preprocessing and feature definitions, frozen model/baseline, outcome-appropriate metrics, conditional uncertainty, transportability and the separate related-trait correction family. Network analysis needs network source/version, nodes/edges, weights, filtering, algorithm and null model. Network preservation needs frozen reference memberships, exact source namespaces/species, complete thresholded edge coverage, matched correlation estimators/thresholds, shared-node coverage and edge/sign metrics. Absent thresholded edges are not zero raw correlations; these descriptive metrics are not preservation P values or independent replication and do not choose the official graph. When a separate conditional network-label null was tested, report its prespecified signed/unsigned edge statistic, shared-node universe, frozen memberships, label-exchangeability rationale and strata, exact group or sampled draw count/seed, tie-inclusive tail, plus-one sampled P, Monte Carlo tail interval, complete module/target denominator and correction. This is conditional topology evidence, not participant-sampling uncertainty, WGCNA Zsummary or an association discovery. Colocalization needs region/build, source selection/export cutoffs, observed pre-restriction variant counts versus alignment candidates, matched fractions and positional gaps, sample sizes, LD, all signal pairs and credible sets, convergence attempts/fallback, registered priors and their complete sensitivity grid. State whether any posterior decision rule was registered; posterior probabilities are not association FDR. Source-declared completeness is not independently certified, and partial-data grades/caveats must accompany every claim. Protein structure methods need exact accession/isoform/taxon and sequence hash/version, assay-to-sequence limitations, observed residue coverage and mapping, retrieval versus newly executed prediction, software/model/seed/MSA/template provenance, all assessed models, pLDDT source and missingness, directional PAE and region/token mapping. Confidence supplies model context and does not establish function, pathogenicity or an interface. Do not infer settings from current software defaults for historical runs, substitute unrelated citations, invent a parameter rationale, or present a query match as verified support. Missing source, parameter or required uncommon-parameter justification remains a review need. Report the dataset tissue/sample compartment for each cohort and consider declared differences when interpreting heterogeneity; do not infer causation from a cohort-confounded tissue contrast. Main Methods explain the scientific design and analyses. Put software versions, resource releases and detailed reproducibility information in Supplementary Methods or availability documentation. Keep internal audit/editorial commentary, hashes and execution histories in separate review records. Include one concise, verified data and code availability statement near the end of the manuscript.";
