ation were performed when they were not. Keep a claim-level evidence ledger for each principal story, distinguishing this study\'s association, a primary source\'s reported results, inferred mechanistic links, hypotheses and experiments proposed for the future. Bind literature claims to the actual retrieved passages and state the source study\'s design, species, tissue, molecular trait, phenotype and limitations. A title or abstract excerpt does not establish that a full article was read. Do not invent inaccessible experimental details. The native finding_review contract checks prose/source bindings and depth facets locally; those checks do not certify scientific truth or approve source-text transmission. Keep a substantial self-contained synthesis and all conclusion-changing caveats in the main text. Put the complete source-linked discussion, evidence/claim ledger, sensitivity details, alternative mechanisms and proposed validation in a linked finding-specific supplement. Do not truncate evidence to meet a provisional equal per-finding allowance. When a study-wide impact assessment exists, use finding_ids to connect each principal story to the same frozen finding in its linked Results paragraphs. Record impact_selection_override_reason for a scientist\'s change to the selected findings or their priority order; excluded findings cannot be revived by an override. Integrate the findings into one coherent answer: explain convergence, complementary evidence and unresolved tension, and how each finding changes the combined interpretation. Shared participants or correlated analyses are not independent confirmation. Do not force discordant results into agreement. Highlight unexpected findings only against a documented study hypothesis or source-supported prior expectation: describe the departure, its implications, alternative explanations and a discriminating test. Label post hoc explanations; omit the surprise claim if no supported expectation exists. Then discuss future_