static String instructions() {
    return "For registered cross-hypothesis MR families, distinguish joint_adjusted_p and joint_family_status from source adjustments. An unresolved joint family establishes no joint MR discoveries. Association significance cannot substitute for MR multiplicity or causal evidence. Begin Results with the native participant-characteristics Table 1, then report applicable analyses in the same order as Methods: association, discovery/replication, meta-analysis, enrichment/ontology, Mendelian randomization, network analysis, fine mapping, colocalization and sensitivity analyses. Use results_role, not impact rank, to order Results. Include important null, discordant and sensitivity results; do not impose a five-paragraph cap. Place relevant bioinformatics evidence alongside the finding it informs, using supporting_evidence entries with source and relationship. Explain the exact feature/isoform/gene, tissue and phenotype match, direction, limitations and whether the evidence supports, contradicts or only contextualizes the finding. For survival findings, distinguish log hazard ratios from odds/risk ratios and absolute risk. Report the endpoint/time-axis, event/censor counts, censoring/PH assumptions and source model. Treat survival_model_context and its separately adjusted or unavailable PH diagnostics as interpretation/sensitivity context, never additional primary discoveries or proof of causality. Preserve the distinction between source LRT P values and subsequent meta-analysis Wald inference. Distinguish finite coefficient existence from calibration and assumption checks; compatible supplied results do not imply a native certificate. Infinite coefficients invalidate ordinary Wald effect inference; a separately justified score or likelihood-ratio P-only result may still be usable under its own protocol.  Do not attach all bioinformatics output to every result or treat a protein structure, sequence annotation, search hit or gene-level paper as isoform-specific causal validation. Begin Discussion with a concise biological answer to the study question, then develop three to five distinct principal findings. Express their importance through the science, without announcing impact ranks or \'the second finding\'. Make a persuasive, evidence-grounded case for why the study was worthwhile: return to the Introduction\'s motivation and consequential gap, compare with the closest primary studies, and explain the specific knowledge added, including replication, refinement or informative null findings when warranted. Novelty adjectives and significance counts cannot establish contribution. Use discussion_role principal_finding, consecutive impact_rank values up to the configured maximum (default 5), result_ids referring to Results paragraph IDs, and an explicit impact_reason reflected in the prose. Rank findings, not analysis types or smallest P-values: weigh effect size and uncertainty, replication, biological relevance, tissue/assay match, sensitivity and contrary evidence. Distinct findings may arise from the same analysis; do not present the same finding three times. If fewer than three defensible findings exist, use fewer stories and record why in discussion_selection_note. Each story entry may contain several connected prose paragraphs. Develop each principal finding thoroughly across as many paragraphs as its evidence requires. Explain the observed effect and uncertainty, exact gene/variant/isoform and tissue, relevant primary studies and their designs/results, the proposed mechanism step by step, which links are demonstrated versus inferred or unresolved, conflicting/null evidence and alternative explanations, practical relevance and concrete next experiments. Aim for the depth of an integrated mechanistic research account such as Wickenhagen et al., Science 2021, doi:10.1126/science.abj3624; this is a depth benchmark, not evidence for a supplied study\'s findings. Never imply that experiments, MR, colocalization or structural validation were performed when they were not. Keep a claim-level evidence ledger for each principal story, distinguishing this study\'s association, a primary source\'s reported results, inferred mechanistic links, hypotheses and experiments proposed for the future. Bind literature claims to the actual retrieved passages and state the source study\'s design, species, tissue, molecular trait, phenotype and limitations. A title or abstract excerpt does not establish that a full article was read. Do not invent inaccessible experimental details. The native finding_review contract checks prose/source bindings and depth facets locally; those checks do not certify scientific truth or approve source-text transmission. Keep a substantial self-contained synthesis and all conclusion-changing caveats in the main text. Put the complete source-linked discussion, evidence/claim ledger, sensitivity details, alternative mechanisms and proposed validation in a linked finding-specific supplement. Do not truncate evidence to meet a provisional equal per-finding allowance. When a study-wide impact assessment exists, use finding_ids to connect each principal story to the same frozen finding in its linked Results paragraphs. Record impact_selection_override_reason for a scientist\'s change to the selected findings or their priority order; excluded findings cannot be revived by an override. Integrate the findings into one coherent answer: explain convergence, complementary evidence and unresolved tension, and how each finding changes the combined interpretation. Shared participants or correlated analyses are not independent confirmation. Do not force discordant results into agreement. Highlight unexpected findings only against a documented study hypothesis or source-supported prior expectation: describe the departure, its implications, alternative explanations and a discriminating test. Label post hoc explanations; omit the surprise claim if no supported expectation exists. Then discuss future_potential, limitations and next_steps, ending with overall_conclusion (either the final Discussion paragraph or the separate Conclusion, not both). Older drafts with next_steps before limitations remain structurally accepted; their argument still requires substantive review. Develop future potential with grounded optimism: connect each promising implication to a finding, explain what it could enable, and name the specific validation needed. Use measured phrases such as \'could help distinguish\' or \'if confirmed, may provide a basis for\'; avoid stacked hedges or cancelling every prospect with a generic disclaimer. Keep applications proportionate to the evidence and proposed work distinct from work performed. For each material limitation, identify the actual design or evidence gap, its consequence for a specific inference and what remains supported; do not guess bias direction or recite generic weaknesses. Connect feasible follow-up to that uncertainty, explain which alternatives its outcomes would distinguish and how they would change the conclusion. Some limitations can only be reduced or need a different design; do not promise to resolve them all. Prioritize the next step by scientific value and the most consequential uncertainty. End by integrating the evidence into the answer to the Introduction\'s question, the supported contribution and its scope, and the next justified question, without new results or stronger causal claims. Before finalizing, audit the Discussion\'s contribution, synthesis, evidence for any surprise and the result-to-limitation-to-next-step reasoning. Editorial review must identify the weakest inference or transition and propose an attributed replacement or specify the evidence needed to repair it. Structural completeness cannot certify persuasiveness or impact. Keep internal versions and audit provenance in review artifacts or a brief supplemental note, outside the scientific Discussion. Keep all colocalization signal pairs and distinguish their actual molecular/outcome traits, registered primary prior and sensitivity range; do not select only the largest H4 or count signal pairs as independent loci. Report observed pre-restriction coverage versus candidate matching and convergence/fallback. Source-declared complete regions are not independently certified, and H4 is not association FDR or causal direction. If any colocalization result has evidence_grade exploratory_partial_region_major_limitation, reproduce its required_manuscript_caveat in the main-text limitations: the posterior is conditional on observed selected variants, incomplete coverage can bias it, and a null result is not evidence against sharing. Cite retrieved cataloged references where appropriate, retain major contradictory findings in the main text, and keep additional detail in the supplement. Never invent results, novelty, causality or drug efficacy to fill the outline. Structural validation is not scientific validation; untagged older prose needs explicit review, not silent rewriting.";
}

