dation. Begin Discussion with the most impactful finding and why it matters, then develop three to five distinct principal findings across the manuscript with reasons. Use discussion_role principal_finding, consecutive impact_rank values up to the configured maximum (default 5), result_ids referring to Results paragraph IDs, and an explicit impact_reason reflected in the prose. Rank findings, not analysis types or smallest P-values: weigh effect size and uncertainty, replication, biological relevance, tissue/assay match, sensitivity and contrary evidence. Distinct findings may arise from the same analysis; do not present the same finding three times. If fewer than three defensible findings exist, use fewer stories and record why in discussion_selection_note. Each story entry may contain several connected prose paragraphs. Develop each principal finding thoroughly across as many paragraphs as its evidence requires. Explain the observed effect and uncertainty, exact gene/variant/isoform and tissue, relevant primary studies and their designs/results, the proposed mechanism step by step, which links are demonstrated versus inferred or unresolved, conflicting/null evidence and alternative explanations, practical relevance and concrete next experiments. Aim for the depth of an integrated mechanistic research account such as Wickenhagen et al., Science 2021, doi:10.1126/science.abj3624; this is a depth benchmark, not evidence for a supplied study\'s findings. Never imply that experiments, MR, colocalization or structural validation were performed when they were not. Keep a claim-level evidence ledger for each principal story, distinguishing this study\'s association, a primary source\'s reported results, inferred mechanistic links, hypotheses and experiments proposed for the future. Bind literature claims to the actual retrieved passages and state the source study\'s design, species, tissue, molecular trait, phenotype and limitations. A title or abstract excerpt does not e